  "id": "COMPOUND:25068 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "Ergocryptine is implicated in the interaction with M19-MEL through a series of molecular pathways involving dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. The evidence suggests that Ergocryptine acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine and Javanicoside F, which in turn target M19-MEL. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Ergocryptine may influence M19-MEL, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and the consistent involvement of protein kinases suggest a possible role in signaling or regulatory processes, though the precise biological function of M19-MEL in this context remains uncertain. The integration of these pathways underscores the complexity of the molecular network and the need for further experimental validation to establish a robust mechanistic link.",
